ok   insert_all returns the ids of the rows it inserted and skips duplicates
ok   returning: names the columns, cast by type; [] and nil return nothing
ok   insert_all! raises on a duplicate
ok   insert_all fills created_at and updated_at once per call, and not with record_timestamps: false
ok   rows with different keys raise before anything is written
ok   an encrypted column is refused in a bulk row
ok   upsert_all updates only the supplied columns and keeps created_at
ok   upsert_all with update_only and returning
ok   a call with more binds than the variable limit is chunked inside one transaction
ok   decimal rounding, json text, Date text and Time format in bulk rows
ok   update_all casts every value by its column's type, as save and the bulk writes do
ok   bulk rows bind a boolean as 1/0 and a binary value as a BLOB
ok   returning:, unique_by: and update_only: take one Symbol or String as one column
ok   false is no columns; any other value for returning:, unique_by: or update_only: raises
